3	// ============================================================================
4	// csrc/fused/sm_90/model_stage_vit.cuh — PHASE 2 of the TRUE L3 fused
5	// megakernel: the REAL Vision-Transformer forward + backward as in-kernel stages
6	// of the persistent megakernel (the ViT counterpart of PHASE 1's decoder
7	// model_stages_decoder.cuh). ONE self-contained header per the portability
8	// contract (csrc/fused/COMPONENT_CONTRACT.md): provides vit forward/backward
9	// stages, includes ONLY the substrate header + CUDA, no globals, no repo build
10	// flags.
11	//
12	// HONESTY: this is the genuine eager architecture (grokking_race_v2.py ViT,
13	// lines 379-404), transcribed LINE-FOR-LINE from the verified PyTorch oracle in
14	// tests/hw/vit_oracle.py, which is asserted bit-identical (fp64, ~1e-15 rel) to
15	// torch.autograd for the loss and EVERY one of the 32 parameter gradients, and
16	// structurally mirrored on CPU in tests/hw/vit_kernel_mirror.py. There is NO
17	// placeholder math on this path. The one deliberate, documented deviation from
18	// the oracle is execution mechanics, not numerics: the backward RECOMPUTES each
19	// layer's forward from the cached layer INPUT (rather than caching every
20	// intermediate) to keep only one layer's activations live in smem at a time —
21	// see the smem-budget note below. The math computed is identical; only the
22	// storage strategy differs.
23	//
24	// ARCHITECTURE (exact; cites grokking_race_v2.py lines):
25	//   ViT(p=97, patch_dim=49, num_patches=16, d=128, h=4, nl=2)
26	//     patch_proj = Linear(49,128) (:392)  — per-patch embed (16 patches)
27	//     cls_token  = Parameter[1,1,128]*.02 (:393) — prepended at position 0
28	//     pos        = Embedding(16+1,128) (:394) — 17 learned position embeds
29	//     2 × EncoderBlock (:379):
30	//       attn = MultiheadAttention(128,4,batch_first) (:382), NO MASK — FULL
31	//              (bidirectional) attention (contrast: decoder is causal).
32	//       n1,n2 = LayerNorm(128) (:383), eps=1e-5 (torch default)
33	//       ff = Linear(128,512) → GELU(exact erf) → Linear(512,128) (:384)
34	//       POST-LN: x=n1(x+attn(x)); h=n2(x+ff(x))  (:386-387)
35	//     norm = LayerNorm(128) (:396); out = Linear(128,97) (:396)
36	//     forward: h=patch_proj(x); h=cat([cls,h]); h+=pos; for l: h=l(h);
37	//              return out(norm(h[:,0,:]))  (:400-404)  — CLS token (pos 0).
38	//   loss = cross_entropy(logits, targets) (mean over batch; :967…).
39	//   INPUT is FLOAT image patches [B,16,49] (NOT int tokens); targets int [B].
40	//
41	// NUMERICS (verified in the oracle; see vit_oracle.py):
42	//   * GELU = exact erf  0.5x(1+erf(x/√2)); grad 0.5(1+erf(x/√2))+x·φ(x),
43	//     φ(x)=(1/√(2π))e^{-x²/2}.
44	//   * LayerNorm eps = 1e-5; dx uses the two mean-correction terms.
45	//   * attention scale 1/√dh = 1/√32; softmax subtracts the row max; FULL (no
46	//     causal triangle — every key position contributes for every query).
47	//   * cross-entropy MEAN over B → dlogits = (softmax−onehot)/B.
48	//
49	// PARALLELIZATION (locked design — Option B, batch-parallel, deterministic;
50	//   identical to the decoder's, see model_stages_decoder.cuh):
51	//   * Each CTA owns a FIXED contiguous batch slice (by blockIdx.x). The whole
52	//     CTA cooperates on ONE sample at a time and iterates its slice SEQUENTIALLY.
53	//   * Per-sample, the CTA accumulates that sample's weight-grad contribution into
54	//     the CTA's OWN partial buffer (gw + cta*total). Each dW element has a SINGLE
55	//     owner thread that does partial[e] += contrib across the slice's samples in
56	//     fixed order (__syncthreads between samples) — single-writer, no atomics,
57	//     deterministic.
58	//   * The cross-CTA reduce + optimizer tail live in fused_vit_megakernel.cuh
59	//     (deterministic ascending-CTA summation order).
60	//
61	// SMEM BUDGET PER CTA — DYNAMIC SHARED MEMORY (one sample, one layer live):
62	//   At seq=17 the per-sample working set is ≈ sizeof(VitSampleSmem) ≈ 180 KB —
63	//   FAR over the 48 KB STATIC __shared__ cap (a static `__shared__ VitSampleSmem`
64	//   would NOT COMPILE). So ViT uses EXTERN/DYNAMIC shared memory: the launcher
65	//   calls cudaFuncSetAttribute(MaxDynamicSharedMemorySize, sizeof(VitSampleSmem))
66	//   and passes dynamicSMemBytes=sizeof(VitSampleSmem) at <<<>>>. 180 KB ≪ the
67	//   sm_90 per-block dynamic-smem cap (227 KB), and the persistent megakernel is
68	//   one-CTA-per-SM BY DESIGN (gridDim=#SMs, grid barrier over #SMs), so occupancy
69	//   =1 IS the design point — a 180 KB block at occ=1 is exactly intended, NOT a
70	//   regression. The dominant buffers are ff0 (pre-GELU) + gact (post-GELU), 34 KB
71	//   each; both kept live within the processed layer (ff0 for gelu'(), gact for
72	//   the dW_ff2 GEMM). The exact byte count is static_asserted in vit_layout.cuh.
73	//   (TODO[bf16]: a bf16-activation variant would roughly halve this and is a
74	//   flagged follow-up defaulting to THIS fp32 path — consistent with the decoder.)
75	// ============================================================================
